{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Elazar the kohen said, etc.</b> Because Moshe came to include anger, he came to include error — for the laws of gentile utensil-immersion were hidden from him. And so you find on the eighth day of inauguration, where it says ״וַיִּקְצֹף עַל אֶלְעָזָר וְעַל אִיתָמָר״ (Leviticus 10) — he came to include anger, he came to include error. And likewise with שִׁמְעוּ נָא הַמֹּרִים (Numbers 20), ״וַיַּךְ אֶת הַסֶּלַע״ — through anger he erred (Sifrei; Pesachim 66b)." "<b>Which YHWH commanded, etc.</b> He attributed the ruling to his teacher (see Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:26.317310804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}